 "notes": "Headline result: left panel of Fig. 3 (COBE/FIRAS gamma->A' constraint on kinetic mixing epsilon vs dark photon mass m_A'), 95% CL. This is the general kinetic-mixing bound from CMB spectral distortions; it does NOT require A' to be dark matter, so dm_density_assumed is null. The paper reports two PDF prescriptions (log-normal, red; analytic, blue); the shaded excluded region is bounded by the more conservative choice, which is the log-normal curve (higher epsilon in the trough, ~2.3e-7 vs ~1.1e-7 analytic). I traced the red log-normal solid curve via pymupdf get_drawings vector extraction, calibrated to the log-log axes (x: 1e-16..1e-9 eV; y: 1e-9..~1e0). The curve is the lower boundary of the excluded region: a near-vertical left wall near m_A'~2e-15 eV, a broad trough (min ~2.3e-7 around 6e-13 eV), a step up to ~2.2e-6 near 3.4e-12 eV (end of homogeneous-limit resonance), then a descending right tail to ~4e-8 at 1e-9 eV. epsilon reported directly (chi), not chi^2. The right panel (He-reionization dark-photon-dark-matter A'->gamma, assuming Omega_A'=Omega_DM) is a separate, stronger DPDM bound not chosen here since it is density/DM-dependent.",
